        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructor for <ref refid="classastrea_1_1astro_1_1StateTransitionMatrix" kindref="compound">StateTransitionMatrix</ref>. Uses the provided equations of motion and state to initialize the STM numerically. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>eom</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Equations of motion object </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>date</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current date </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>state</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current orbital elements state vector </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>vehicle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="classastrea_1_1astro_1_1Vehicle" kindref="compound">Vehicle</ref> object </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>f(s) = [f0(s), f1(s), ..., fn(s)] where fi is the ith component of the equations of motion</para>
<para>df/ds = |df0/ds0, df0/ds1, ..., df0/dsn| where dfi/ds is the partial derivative of the ith component with respect to the state vector |df1/ds0, df1/ds1, ..., df1/dsn| | ... | |dfn/ds0, dfn/ds1, ..., dfn/dsn|</para>
<para>df/dsi = f(s + dsi) - f(s) / dsi units = (OEP - OEP)/OEi = OEP/OEi -&gt; i.e. [da/dt]/[a], [de/dt]/[a], [di/dt]/[a], [dOmega/dt]/[a], [domega/dt]/[a], [dM/dt]/[a]</para>
<para>It might be possible to use fancy metaprogramming to deduce the units of each element based on the element type but that seems like a huge headache. For now, we force the elements into unitless quantities, converted using their underlying units, and then force a conversion back. This makes this function implicity unsafe from a unit perspective.</para>
        </inbodydescription>
